ion</label><label><input name="q45" type="radio" value="3"/> <b>D.</b> MPLS labeling</label><button onclick="cq(45)">Check Answer</button><div class="feedback" id="f45"></div><span id="r45" style="display:none">Correct answer: Endpoint identity-to-location control-plane mapping. The distractors act at a different protocol layer or policy stage.</span></div><div class="q"><span class="badge">Historical</span><h3>46. SD-Access fabric data plane?</h3><label><input name="q46" type="radio" value="0"/> <b>A.</b> RIP</label><label><input name="q46" type="radio" value="1"/> <b>B.</b> VXLAN</label><label><input name="q46" type="radio" value="2"/> <b>C.</b> LDP</label><label><input name="q46" type="radio" value="3"/> <b>D.</b> GRE only</label><button onclick="cq(46)">Check Answer</button><div class="feedback" id="f46"></div><span id="r46" style="display:none">Correct answer: VXLAN. The distractors act at a different protocol layer or policy stage.</span></div><div class="q"><span class="badge">Historical</span><h3>47. RIB versus FIB?</h3><label><input name="q47" type="radio" value="0"/> <b>A.</b> Identical</label><label><input name="q47" type="radio" value="1"/> <b>B.</b> RIB L2 only</label><label><input name="q47" type="radio" value="2"/> <b>C.</b> RIB is route selection/control; FIB is programmed forwarding</label><label><input name="q47" type="radio" value="3"/> <b>D.</b> FIB BGP only</label><button onclick="cq(47)">Check Answer</button><div class="feedback" id="f47"></div><span id="r47" style="display:none">Correct answer: RIB is route selection/control; FIB is programmed forwarding. The distractors act at a different protocol layer or policy stage.</span></div><div class="q"><span class="badge">Historical</span><h3>48. BUM stands for what?</h3><label><input name="q48" type="radio" value="0"/> <b>A.</b> BGP, Underlay, MPLS</label><label><input name="q48" type="radio" value="1"/> <b>B.</b> Bridge, Unicast, Metric</label><label><input name="q48" type="radio" value="2"/> <b>C.</b> Backup, Uplink, Multihop</label><label><input name="q48" type="radio" value="3"/> <b>D.</b> Broadcast, Unknown-unicast, Multicast</label><button onclick="cq(48)">Check Answer</button><div class="feedback" id="f48"></div><span id="r48" style="display:none">Correct answer: Broadcast, Unknown-unicast, Multicast. The distractors act at a different protocol layer or policy stage.</span></div><div class="q"><span class="badge">Historical</span><h3>49. Strong troubleshooting order?</h3><label><input name="q49" type="radio" value="0"/> <b>A.</b> Adjacency → route/RIB → recursion/FIB → encapsulation/policy → packet test</label><label><input name="q49" type="radio" value="1"/> <b>B.</b> Packet only</label><label><input name="q49" type="radio" value="2"/> <b>C.</b> GUI then reboot</label><label><input name="q49" type="radio" value="3"/> <b>D.</b> STP then DNS</label><button onclick="cq(49)">Check Answer</button><div class="feedback" id="f49"></div><span id="r49" style="display:none">Correct answer: Adjacency → route/RIB → recursion/FIB → encapsulation/policy → packet test. The distractors act at a different protocol layer or policy stage.</span></div><div class="q"><span class="badge">Historical</span><h3>50. Policy migration between vendors: map what first?</h3><label><input name="q50" type="radio" value="0"/> <b>A.</b> Exact syntax</label><label><input name="q50" type="radio" value="1"/> <b>B.</b> Intent and policy attachment stage</label><label><input name="q50" type="radio" value="2"/> <b>C.</b> Interface names</label><label><input name="q50" type="radio" value="3"/> <b>D.</b> Hostname</label><button onclick="cq(50)">Check Answer</button><div class="feedback" id="f50"></div><span id="r50" style="display:none">Correct answer: Intent and policy attachment stage. The distractors act at a different protocol layer or policy stage.</span></div><h2>Source index</h2><section class="card"><ol><li><b>Cisco — Hierarchical eBGP EVPN multihoming</b><br/><a href="https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst_standalones/Multihoming/multihoming-in-bgp-evpn-vxlan-fabric/hierarchical-multihoming/configure-ebgp-based-evpn-multihoming-and-fabric-network.html">https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst_standalones/Multihoming/multihoming-in-bgp-evpn-vxlan-fabric/hierarchical-multihoming/configure-ebgp-based-evpn-multihoming-and-fabric-network.html</a></li><li><b>Cisco — All-active EVPN multihoming consistency</b><br/><a href="https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst_standalones/Multihoming/multihoming-in-bgp-evpn-vxlan-fabric/all-active-mode/restriction-for-aa-multihoming.html">https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst_standalones/Multihoming/multihoming-in-bgp-evpn-vxlan-fabric/all-active-mode/restriction-for-aa-multihoming.html</a></li><li><b>Cisco — Routed overlay and IRB mapping boundaries</b><br/><a href="https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst_standalones/Multihoming/multihoming-in-bgp-evpn-vxlan-fabric/routed-overlay-mh/routed-overlay-network-reference-configuration.html">https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst_standalones/Multihoming/multihoming-in-bgp-evpn-vxlan-fabric/routed-overlay-mh/routed-overlay-network-reference-configuration.html</a></li><li><b>Fortinet — BGP multipath before SD-WAN steering</b><br/><a href="https://community.fortinet.com/fortigate-3/technical-tip-configuring-sd-wan-traffic-steering-with-bgp-learned-routes-229549">https://community.fortinet.com/fortigate-3/technical-tip-configuring-sd-wan-traffic-steering-with-bgp-learned-routes-229549</a></li><li><b>Fortinet — Performance SLA when BGP remains Established</b><br/><a href="https://community.fortinet.com/fortigate-3/technical-tip-using-sd-wan-performance-sla-to-steer-traffic-when-bgp-remains-established-229544">https://community.fortinet.com/fortigate-3/technical-tip-using-sd-wan-performance-sla-to-steer-traffic-when-bgp-remains-established-229544</a></li><li><b>Fortinet — OSPF tags redistributed into BGP</b><br/><a href="https://community.fortinet.com/fortigate-3/technical-tip-wrong-route-tag-added-to-bgp-routes-redistributed-from-ospf-214352">https://community.fortinet.com/fortigate-3/technical-tip-wrong-route-tag-added-to-bgp-routes-redistributed-from-ospf-214352</a></li><li><b>Palo Alto Networks — Advanced Routing Engine filter attachment points</b><br/><a href="https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/networking/advanced-routing/create-filters-for-the-advanced-routing-engine">https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/networking/advanced-routing/create-filters-for-the-advanced-routing-engine</a></li><li><b>Palo Alto Networks — OSPF migration exceptions</b><br/><a href="https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/pan-os/u-v/routing-engine-migration-reference/routing-protocol-migration-exceptions/ospf">https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/pan-os/u-v/routing-engine-migration-reference/routing-protocol-migration-exceptions/ospf</a></li><li><b>Palo Alto Networks — Redistribution versus BGP export</b><br/><a href="https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/networking/configure-route-redistribution">https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/networking/configure-route-redistribution</a></li><li><b>Arista Networks — EVPN Type-5 DCI re-origination</b><br/><a href="https://www.arista.com/en/um-eos/eos-configuring-evpn">https://www.arista.com/en/um-eos/eos-configuring-evpn</a></li><li><b>Arista Networks — Single-gateway centralized routing and BUM</b><br/><a href="https://www.arista.com/en/um-eos/eos-evpn-vxlan-single-gateway-centralized-routing">https://www.arista.com/en/um-eos/eos-evpn-vxlan-single-gateway-centralized-routing</a></li><li><b>Arista Networks — Control plane versus data plane</b><br/><a href="https://www.arista.com/en/um-eos/eos-data-transfer">https://www.arista.com/en/um-eos/eos-data-transfer</a></li><li><b>Aruba/HPE — VSX logical VTEP with independent BGP speakers</b><br/><a href="https://www.arubanetworks.com/techdocs/AOS-CX/10.15/PDF/vsx.pdf">https://www.arubanetworks.com/techdocs/AOS-CX/10.15/PDF/vsx.pdf</a></li><li><b>Aruba/HPE — OSPF redistribution and active-routes-only</b><br/><a href="https://www.arubanetworks.com/techdocs/AOS-CX/10.15/PDF/ip_route_6300-6400-8100-83xx-9300-10000.pdf">https://www.arubanetworks.com/techdocs/AOS-CX/10.15/PDF/ip_route_6300-6400-8100-83xx-9300-10000.pdf</a></li><li><b>Aruba/HPE — Layered VXLAN troubleshooting with VSX</b><br/><a href="https://www.arubanetworks.com/techdocs/AOS-CX/10.15/PDF/vsx.pdf">https://www.arubanetworks.com/techdocs/AOS-CX/10.15/PDF/vsx.pdf</a></li><li><b>Juniper — EVPN-VXLAN with IPv6 underlay</b><br/><a href="https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/evpn/topics/topic-map/vxlan-ipv6-underlay-overview.html">https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/evpn/topics/topic-map/vxlan-ipv6-underlay-overview.html</a></li><li><b>Juniper — Routing protocols on EVPN IRB</b><br/><a href="https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/evpn/topics/concept/protocols-evpn-vxlan.html">https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/evpn/topics/concept/protocols-evpn-vxlan.html</a></li><li><b>Juniper — Type-5 subnet routes for scale</b><br/><a href="https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/release-notes/25.4/junos-release-notes-25.4r1/topics/new-features/feature-descriptions/evpn-9.html">https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/release-notes/25.4/junos-release-notes-25.4r1/topics/new-features/feature-descriptions/evpn-9.html</a></li><li><b>FRRouting — EVPN depends on Linux bridge/VRF state</b><br/><a href="https://docs.frrouting.org/en/latest/evpn.html">https://docs.frrouting.org/en/latest/evpn.html</a></li><li><b>FRRouting — OSPF redistribution by area type</b><br/><a href="https://docs.frrouting.org/en/latest/ospfd.html">https://docs.frrouting.org/en/latest/ospfd.html</a></li><li><b>FRRouting — IS-IS Segment Routing capability matrix</b><br/><a href="https://docs.frrouting.org/en/stable-10.0/isisd.html">https://docs.frrouting.org/en/stable-10.0/isisd.html</a></li></ol><p>Run timestamp: 2026-08-29-08-11. Community material is labeled by source; release-specific official documentation should prevail when behavior differs.</p></section><script>const A={},M={};function cq(n){let s=document.querySelector('input[name=q'+n+']:checked'),f=document.getElementById('f'+n);f.style.display='block';if(!s){f.innerHTML='Select an answer first.';return}let ok=+s.value===A[n];M[n].checked=true;f.className='feedback '+(ok?'good':'bad');f.innerHTML=(ok?'<b>Correct.</b> ':'<b>Incorrect.</b> ')+document.getElementById('r'+n).textContent+'<br><b>What you missed:</b> '+(ok?'Correct state boundary identified.':'Find the first missing state before selecting a fix.')}function grade(){let c=0,a=0,ch=0,b={};Object.keys(A).forEach(k=>{let n=+k,s=document.querySelector('input[name=q'+n+']:checked'),d=M[n].domain;b[d]??=[0,0];b[d][1]++;if(M[n].checked)ch++;if(s){a++;if(+s.value===A[n]){c++;b[d][0]++}}});let p=Math.round(c/50*100),rows=Object.entries(b).map(([d,v])=>'<tr><td>'+d+'</td><td>'+v[0]+'/'+v[1]+'</td></tr>').join('');document.getElementById('score').innerHTML=(p>=80?'PASS':'FAIL')+' — '+c+'/50 ('+p+'%) • Answered '+a+'/50 • Checked '+ch+'/50<table><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Correct</th></tr>'+rows+'</table>'}function reset(){document.querySelectorAll('.q input').forEach(x=>x.checked=false);document.querySelectorAll('.feedback').forEach(x=>x.style.display='none');Object.keys(M).forEach(k=>M[k].checked=false);document.getElementById('score').innerHTML=''}function badimg(i){i.style.display='none';i.parentElement.parentElement.querySelector('.fb').style.display='block'}Object.assign(A,{"1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3, "5": 0, "6": 1, "7": 2, "8": 3, "9": 0, "10": 1, "11": 2, "12": 3, "13": 0, "14": 1, "15": 2, "16": 3, "17": 0, "18": 1, "19": 2, "20": 3, "21": 0, "22": 1, "23": 2, "24": 3, "25": 0, "26": 1, "27": 2, "28": 3, "29": 0, "30": 1, "31": 2, "32"